{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780024932,"nonce":"DTZNQuM3cc4gEbkKjyLIKSww+e8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDu2Bmw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/196","origin":"github"},"title":"Capture external-charger idle/maintenance current (~6.2 A, #186) + revisit power models","message":"## Summary\n\nDuring deployment #186 (2026-05-28), after the boat had been on the charger for several days since the prior deployment, the **external charger read ~6.2 A draw** — operator's interpretation: covering the idle/maintenance load at/near full charge. Capture this in the power data and revisit the power model(s) with it.\n\n## Why this datapoint matters\n\nBizzyBoat has **no in-line current meter** — `BatteryState.current` reads ~0.01 A (placeholder); only voltage is real. So **external-charger current readings are the only real current measurements we get** on this hull. A measured idle/maintenance draw is therefore rare and valuable: the prior comprehensive power analysis ([#167](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/167), the 2026-05-19 → 21 → 22 single-charge discharge cycle) was discharge-side and current-free (voltage + coulomb-counting inference). This is a charge/idle-side **measured-current** anchor.\n\nRecharge-to-full time is the binding cohort-cadence constraint (batteries are charged in place, not field-swapped), so charger-draw characterization feeds deployment cadence planning.\n\n## Asks\n\n- [ ] Record the ~6.2 A datapoint in the power data record (with charger model/setup + the multi-day-charged context; note it's an operator-read external-charger value, not logged telemetry).\n- [ ] Revisit the power model(s) from #167 with this idle/maintenance-load anchor — does it reconcile with the inferred idle draw, and does it tighten recharge-time estimates?\n- [ ] Consider whether/how to **log charger current** going forward, so these aren't just operator eyeball reads.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Detail in the #186 dev log (2026-05-28, 11:55 pre-launch entry).\n- That dev log currently cross-references this capture to #88, but **#88 is dynamics calibration** (PWM→speed→V-drop), not power — this issue is the correct home; the dev-log reference will be corrected to point here.\n- Part of the Power / endurance roadmap thread.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8`","files":null}]}